Week 1: Static Structural Analysis of a Beam under UDL
Objective: To analyze the stress distribution and deformation characteristics of a structural beam subjected to a Uniformly Distributed Load (UDL).
Boundary Conditions: * Fixed Support: Applied to restrict all degrees of freedom at the support points.
Loading: Uniformly Distributed Load (UDL) and point Force application.
Displacement: Defined constraints to simulate real-world mounting conditions.
Results Obtained: * Equivalent (Von-Mises) Stress: Identified regions of maximum stress concentration to validate safety factors.
Directional Deformation: Analyzed the vertical deflection profile of the beam under the applied load.
